  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "6656188",
      "title": "Understanding ngSwitch",
      "lectureOrder": 425,
      "videoOrder": 391,
      "sourceHash": "f17cf72a1b8098f360688d28b8b9ea9f7966cd30f1eb8f98644ab25c03354c83",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.34,
          "end": 3.93,
          "en": "-: I want to conclude the section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.93,
          "end": 7.14,
          "en": "with one of our built in structural directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.14,
          "end": 11.1,
          "en": "which might be handy from time to time, ngSwitch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.1,
          "end": 15.57,
          "en": "Imagine the case that we have a value like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.57,
          "end": 18.51,
          "en": "which is simply 10.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.51,
          "end": 20.19,
          "en": "Anything you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.19,
          "end": 24.54,
          "en": "Now we got a place in our app where this value changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.54,
          "end": 26.46,
          "en": "and we got a couple of different messages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.46,
          "end": 30.87,
          "en": "we want to display for each of these values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.87,
          "end": 34.86,
          "en": "For this, we can use ngSwitch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.86,
          "end": 37.44,
          "en": "So, let's add a new div here below our paragraphs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.44,
          "end": 40.32,
          "en": "with our own attribute directives.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.32,
          "end": 42.96,
          "en": "And ngSwitch is used like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.96,
          "end": 46.2,
          "en": "We bind to ngSwitch with property binding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.2,
          "end": 48.12,
          "en": "so no star at this point.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.12,
          "end": 49.65,
          "en": "And we bind to value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.65,
          "end": 52.77,
          "en": "So this is our condition basically, what we want to check.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.77,
          "end": 54,
          "en": "And then you might be aware",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54,
          "end": 57.36,
          "en": "that Switch has a couple of cases we can now cover.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.36,
          "end": 60.81,
          "en": "So let's say we have a paragraph where we say value is five.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.81,
          "end": 62.52,
          "en": "Then we have to same for 10.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.52,
          "end": 67.29,
          "en": "Then we have to same for 100 and maybe for default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.29,
          "end": 70.02,
          "en": "Now we need to add something to these paragraphs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.02,
          "end": 72.42,
          "en": "to control which paragraph gets shown",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.42,
          "end": 75.093,
          "en": "because it should only be one of these at a time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.96000000000001,
          "end": 78.46000000000001,
          "en": "That something is ngSwitchCase",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.49,
          "end": 83.61,
          "en": "and we simply pass the value for this case here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.61,
          "end": 86.49,
          "en": "as an argument, for example five.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.49,
          "end": 88.2,
          "en": "And we need to start at the beginning.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 88.2,
          "end": 89.58,
          "en": "That's super important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.58,
          "end": 91.98,
          "en": "So here the star comes into play again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 91.98,
          "end": 93.15,
          "en": "because behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93.15,
          "end": 96.72,
          "en": "this is then all transformed by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 96.72,
          "end": 100.22999999999999,
          "en": "So now we can use this here for the average use cases too,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.22999999999999,
          "end": 104.43,
          "en": "with 10 and with 100.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 104.43,
          "end": 106.56,
          "en": "And finally, for the default case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 106.56,
          "end": 111.56,
          "en": "we have ngSwitchDefault, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.6,
          "end": 115.25999999999999,
          "en": "Now here we also need to add the star, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.25999999999999,
          "end": 118.74000000000001,
          "en": "With this in place, if we save this we only see 10 here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 118.74000000000001,
          "end": 120.09,
          "en": "And if I go to my component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 120.09,
          "end": 124.23,
          "en": "and I change this to five, like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 124.23,
          "end": 126.18,
          "en": "then of course we see five.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 126.18,
          "end": 128.58,
          "en": "So this is ngSwitch, super easy to use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 128.58,
          "end": 130.23,
          "en": "might be useful in some cases",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 130.23,
          "end": 134.07,
          "en": "where you find yourself creating a lot of ngIf conditions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 134.07,
          "end": 138,
          "en": "ngSwitch might be the better solution in such cases.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 138,
          "end": 141.42000000000002,
          "en": "So that is structural directives finished",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 141.42000000000002,
          "end": 143.88,
          "en": "and that is directives overall finished.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 143.88,
          "end": 145.56,
          "en": "You learned a lot about them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 145.56,
          "end": 147.39,
          "en": "and I hope this knowledge allows you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 147.39,
          "end": 150.32999999999998,
          "en": "to create awesome directives for your applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 150.32999999999998,
          "end": 154.02,
          "en": "in cases where the built in ones aren't everything you need,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 154.02,
          "end": 156.18,
          "en": "even though these already cover",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 156.18,
          "end": 158.76,
          "en": "a lot of the default use cases to be honest.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 158.76,
          "end": 160.32,
          "en": "So, let's move on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 160.32,
          "end": 162.6,
          "en": "Let's add a directive to our recipe book",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 162.6,
          "end": 163.92000000000002,
          "en": "in the next section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 163.92000000000002,
          "end": 165.99,
          "en": "and then let's move on in the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
